<?xml version="1.0"?>
<package>
	<metadata>
		<id>ImranAkram.XTB.AutoDeployer</id>
		<version>1.0.0</version>
		<title>Auto Deployer Tool for XrmToolBox</title>
		<authors>Imran Akram, Jonas Rapp, Oleksii Shytikov</authors>
		<owners>imranakram, rappen, biznamics</owners>
		<projectUrl>https://github.com/ImranAkram/XrmToolBox.AutoDeployer</projectUrl>
		<icon>icon.png</icon>
		<readme>docs\README.md</readme>
		<requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
		<description>Tool to automatically upload plugin assemblies and web resources if they are changed during build process.</description>
		<summary>Tool to automatically upload plugin assemblies and web resources if they are changed during build process.</summary>
		<releaseNotes>
- Project files (thanks Jonas Rapp): save the list of watched plugin assemblies, plugin packages and web resources to an .adproj file, and open it again later or on another connection.
- Watched plugin assemblies are now remembered per connection and come back on reconnect, like plugin packages and web resources.
- Opening a project asks whether to keep or replace the current watchers. Replacing now really stops the old watchers.
- Plugin packages: if the saved package id doesn't exist in the connected environment, the package is found by name and the upload is retried.
- Plugin packages in a project are skipped on environments that don't support them (on-premises).
- Fixed: removing a plugin assembly that wasn't found in Dataverse threw an error.
- Built, tested and released with GitHub Actions.
		</releaseNotes>
		<copyright>Copyright 2016-2026 Imran, Jonas, Oleksii</copyright>
		<tags>XrmToolBox Plugins Auto Deployer Tool</tags>
		<dependencies>
			<dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.7.71" />
		</dependencies>
	</metadata>
	<files>
		<file src="XrmToolBox.AutoDeployer\bin\Release\ImranAkram.XTB.AutoDeployer.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins" />
		<file src="icon.png" target="" />
		<file src="README.md" target="docs\" />
	</files>
</package>